__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# QA run artefacts must never be committed to a public skill repo:
# findings reference real builds, hosts, tenants and keys.
# Scoped to the repo root: a QA engagement's own register must never be committed, but the
# fixtures' GENERATED views under tests/fixtures/ are deliberate artifacts. Unscoped, this
# rule silently excluded them and a clone got half a fixture.
/qa-state.json
*-findings.md
.qa-secrets/

# The default report directory, and any hub inside one. The three patterns above state the
# right intent and did not cover this: a hub event log from a scratch run was committed and
# pushed to a public repo before anyone noticed. Root-scoped for the same reason as
# /qa-state.json -- the fixtures under tests/fixtures/ are deliberate.
/qa-reports/
/hub/

# Eval run artefacts: reports and per-run JSON are outputs, not source.
evals/results/

# The secrets directory the method actually names (principles.md section 8).
.product-secrets/
